{
 "definitions": {
  "classes": [
   "PUBLIC",
   "INTERNAL",
   "RESTRICTED"
  ],
  "invariants": [
   [
    "I1",
    "NO_STALE_EFFECT",
    "for every attack scenario and every interleaving of its steps, the full gateway produces no effect the oracle judges prohibited or stale",
    "supported sink (conditional, atomic with the gateway), revocation feed up, authoritative clock"
   ],
   [
    "I2",
    "BENIGN_LIVENESS",
    "for every benign scenario and every interleaving, the expected effect occurs exactly as expected, with a re-approval only where the state really changed",
    "same as I1"
   ],
   [
    "I3",
    "UNKNOWN_NOT_VERIFIED",
    "where the sink cannot be conditioned or applies the effect later, every violating interleaving is reported UNKNOWN by the gateway; none is reported as a verified success",
    "external sinks U01, U02"
   ],
   [
    "I4",
    "FAIL_CLOSED",
    "with the revocation feed offline the gateway never produces an effect on a revoked approval; it returns UNKNOWN",
    "feed offline scenarios F01, F02"
   ],
   [
    "I5",
    "SINGLE_COMMIT",
    "for concurrent writers from one base version exactly one commits (compare-and-swap); no lost update is recorded",
    "A10"
   ]
  ],
  "rules0": {
   "dest.intra.test": {
    "internal": true,
    "ips": [
     "10.0.1.1"
    ]
   },
   "dest.partner.test": {
    "internal": false,
    "ips": [
     "10.0.0.5"
    ]
   },
   "export.INTERNAL": {
    "allow": true,
    "internal_dest_only": true
   },
   "export.PUBLIC": {
    "allow": true
   },
   "export.RESTRICTED": {
    "allow": true,
    "needs_scope": "restricted-export"
   },
   "import.PUBLIC": {
    "allow": true
   }
  },
  "scenarios": [
   [
    "A01",
    "attack",
    "after approval the document is reclassified from PUBLIC to RESTRICTED; the queued export still runs",
    [],
    false,
    false
   ],
   [
    "A02",
    "attack",
    "after approval the document content is replaced by sensitive content (same class)",
    [],
    false,
    false
   ],
   [
    "A03",
    "attack",
    "the principal's export grant is revoked after approval; the queued job still runs with the old credentials",
    [],
    false,
    false
   ],
   [
    "A04",
    "attack",
    "policy is tightened after approval (PUBLIC exports disabled)",
    [],
    false,
    false
   ],
   [
    "A05",
    "attack",
    "the queued job is dispatched long after the approval expired",
    [],
    false,
    false
   ],
   [
    "A06",
    "attack",
    "the same approval is replayed under a new request id (second export)",
    [],
    false,
    false
   ],
   [
    "A07",
    "attack",
    "DNS rebinding: the approved host resolves to a different address when the connection is made",
    [],
    false,
    false
   ],
   [
    "A08",
    "attack",
    "the approved host starts redirecting to a host the policy does not allow",
    [],
    false,
    false
   ],
   [
    "A09",
    "attack",
    "agent B presents agent A's token (handoff without re-approval); B holds no export grant",
    [],
    false,
    false
   ],
   [
    "A10",
    "attack",
    "two writers update the same object from the same base version (conflicting commits)",
    [],
    false,
    false
   ],
   [
    "A11",
    "attack",
    "time skew: the dispatch worker's clock is 80 s behind and accepts an expired token",
    [],
    false,
    false
   ],
   [
    "A12",
    "attack",
    "the approver cancels the approval after issuing it; the queued export still runs",
    [],
    false,
    false
   ],
   [
    "A13",
    "attack",
    "a token issued for one object is used for another (INTERNAL object to an external host)",
    [],
    false,
    false
   ],
   [
    "B01",
    "benign",
    "unchanged object, approved export succeeds",
    [
     {
      "actor": "agentA",
      "host": "partner.test",
      "obj": "doc1"
     }
    ],
    true,
    false
   ],
   [
    "B02",
    "benign",
    "the document is legitimately edited after approval; the operation re-obtains approval and succeeds (a re-approval is justified)",
    [
     {
      "actor": "agentA",
      "host": "partner.test",
      "obj": "doc1"
     }
    ],
    false,
    true
   ],
   [
    "B03",
    "benign",
    "unrelated state changes (other rule, other object, other principal's grant) must not invalidate the approval",
    [
     {
      "actor": "agentA",
      "host": "partner.test",
      "obj": "doc1"
     }
    ],
    true,
    false
   ],
   [
    "B04",
    "benign",
    "queued dispatch well within the approval's lifetime",
    [
     {
      "actor": "agentA",
      "host": "partner.test",
      "obj": "doc1"
     }
    ],
    true,
    false
   ],
   [
    "B05",
    "benign",
    "stable DNS, and a redirect to another host the policy allows",
    [
     {
      "actor": "agentA",
      "host": "partner.test",
      "obj": "doc1"
     }
    ],
    true,
    false
   ],
   [
    "B06",
    "benign",
    "retry with the same request id after the response was lost: one effect, same result",
    [
     {
      "actor": "agentA",
      "host": "partner.test",
      "obj": "doc1"
     }
    ],
    true,
    false
   ],
   [
    "B07",
    "benign",
    "a job is handed from agent A to agent B, which obtains its own approval",
    [
     {
      "actor": "agentB",
      "host": "partner.test",
      "obj": "doc1"
     }
    ],
    true,
    false
   ],
   [
    "B08",
    "benign",
    "concurrent writers on different objects (no conflict), and an unrelated export",
    [
     {
      "actor": "agentA",
      "host": "partner.test",
      "obj": "doc3"
     }
    ],
    true,
    false
   ],
   [
    "B09",
    "benign",
    "dispatch one second before the approval expires",
    [
     {
      "actor": "agentA",
      "host": "partner.test",
      "obj": "doc1"
     }
    ],
    true,
    false
   ],
   [
    "B10",
    "benign",
    "dispatch just after expiry: the operation re-obtains approval and succeeds (a re-approval is justified)",
    [
     {
      "actor": "agentA",
      "host": "partner.test",
      "obj": "doc1"
     }
    ],
    true,
    true
   ],
   [
    "U01",
    "unknown",
